USER Problem:
I have a goal, but i don't know how to break it into manageable steps or stay consistent.
App’s job:
	•	Reduce overwhelm
	•	Provide clarity
	•	Create momentum

AI’s job:
	•	Do the thinking the user struggles with


MVP Core Use Case

User creats a task with:
1. A goal (free text)
2. Target completion date
3. Pacing preference:
   . Daily
   . Weekly

AI does:
1.Interprets the goal
2. Breaks it into small, realistic goals.
3. Distributes steps across times.
4. Returns a plan, not just text.

Normal todo apps:
	•	User must already know what to do

Our app:
	•	User only needs to know what they want
	•	AI figures out how to get there


AI Output Contract Design
1. Define what AI is allowed to return.
2. Making the output stable,predictable and storage ready.
3. Ensure future AI changes doesn't break out APP.

Define strict output schema before implementation
1. Goal Object.
   "goal":{
      "originalText":".....",
      "interpretedText":"......."
   }
   a. user words are preserved exactly.
   b. we can inspect how AI interpreted them.
   c. can be used for regeneration later.

2. Plan Object:
   "plan":{
      "pacing":"daily",
      "startDate":".....",
      "targetDate":".....",
      "steps":12
   }
   a. time logic becomes data.
   b. 

3.  step Object:
   "step":{
      "stepNumber":1,
      "title":"...",
      "description":".....",
      "scheduleDate":".....",
      "estimatedTimeEffort":"........."
   }



API Work flow 
1. Trigger
   User creates a task with:
   . a goal
   . Target completion date
   . Pacing preference(Daily/Weekly)
   ->Backend receives the request -> Calls AI service to generate the subtasks

2. Flow OverView
   a. Backend receives Task creation request
      .Validates input
      .Stores goal first and then attach subtasks after AI returns them.
   b. Backend sends goal to AI service.
      .Include goal text, target date,pacing.
      .Provide any extra metadata(user Id, existing task Id id needed)
   c. AI returns structured plan
      .Follows the output structure form step 1(goal summary + step array)
   d. Backend Parses AI response
      .check structure(all steps have title + time slots)
      .Map each step to task model.
      .Assingn actual dates based on pacing and target data.
      .Save each step in DB.
   e. Backend responses to frontend
      .Includes
         .task ID
         .steps array
         .goal summary

Important Considerations
.Indempotency
   .If user submists same goal twice -> don't duplicate steps.
.Error handling
   .AI fails -> Backend can fall back
      .returns main task only
      .retry
.Pacing
   .Backend converts AI relative time(day1,week2) -> absolute dates
.Step Metadata
   .Include optional fields: estimated effors, dependencies
.Extensibility
   .Keeps AI response parsing isolated -> easier to swap AI model later.

